        "avatar": null,
        "isUploader": false,
        "isVerified": false
      },
      "text": "Therapy for MS is aimed at regulating the immune system. When the patient has an attack, its intensity is regulated by hormonal drugs. If the exacerbation of multiple sclerosis is severe, plasmapheresis can be used, which helps remove antibodies from the blood. Outside of periods of deterioration, patients take drugs that change the course of multiple sclerosis. They are called by the abbreviation PITRS. There are more than 15 types of such drugs, and their use is mandatory for patients. A doctor selects the appropriate PITRS for each patient. In the later stages, a complex combination of drugs is prescribed, including cytostatics, which slow the growth, development and division of cells. In addition, some patients may be prescribed drugs to combat symptoms in order to improve a person's quality of life.\n\n@myheadisempty I hope I helped you!",
